                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "I'm so disappointed in this game, it looked so amazing, the art style, and presentaiton, the trailer looked nice.\nWhat they don't tell you is how it actually plays?\nThis is a PLATFORMER, and you can't jump unless you hammer the M key a bunch to fill aa meter, to allow you to jump.\nonly keyboard controls, but for some reason, all menus ( including restarting after you die ) are on screen clickable buttons with mouse only.\nTHis is the most un-intuitive game I have played in a long time, andI'm including QWOP. \nSo you fill you meter to let you jump, and find you have as much control over your character's jumps as you do controlling an object with your mind ( ie; none ) \nI died 7 times ina row in the TUTORIAL level, andevery time you die, you have to take both hands off the keyboard, abd grab the mouse to click an option to keep playong, or quit. \nIf its THIS bad in the TUTORIAL, there's no way this game is fun in any capacity in the real game.\nNOne of this is explained well, and why are you hammering M to fill a meter to JUMP in a PLATFORMER? that is literally the worst thing ver created for a genre that literally revolves around jumping.\n\nno style\nno grace\nnot even a funny face.\n\nthumbs down, I refunded this immediately.\n",
                        "timestamp_created": 1547680340,
                        "timestamp_updated": 1547680340,
